      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly exhausting to feel like you have already given everything to heal and still feel like collateral damage, and your grief over not being enough does not fit on a standard assessment form. While professionals offer tools, they cannot fix the emotional devastation that makes you question your very existence, which is why feeling like the foundation has collapsed is so disorienting. Please know that your worth is not defined by your ability to function or fix what is broken, and it is safe to stop pretending everything is okay when it isn't. Sometimes the bravest thing you can do is to sit with this wreckage without trying to glue it back together for days or weeks just to let yourself grieve the loss of the person you feel you used to be.",
